i.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":345,"closed_issues":2336,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-07T10:45:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T18:43:23Z","closed_at":"2026-10-08T18:43:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Not reproducible in 4.8.dev2 and earlier\n- Reproducible on 4.8.dev3 and later\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7688) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12600KF (16 threads) - 31.81 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nUnder specific circumstances, trying to assign a C# Resource (class created and used in C#) from GDScript will give the `Cannot assign a new value to a constant.` error.\nFor this error to happen, the C# class must inherit from `Resource` (`RefCounted`, `GodotObject` and `Node` don't give this error), must have the `[GlobalClass]` attribute, and when defined in another class, must have `[Export]`\n\nThis is honestly really confusing to describe, so I'll just give a small code example:\n```cs\n// res://MyResource.cs\n[GlobalClass] // Must be a [GlobalClass] for the error to happen\npublic partial class MyResource : Resource { } // Must be a Resource for the error to happen\n\n// res://MyOtherClass.cs\n[GlobalClass]\npublic partial class MyOtherClass : Node // The type this class inherits from doesn't matter\n{\n    [Export] public MyResource MyRes; // Must have [Export] for the error to happen\n}\n```\n```gdscript\nextends Node\nfunc _ready():\n   var test := MyOtherClass.new()\n   test.MyRes = null # Cannot assign a new value to a constant.\n   test.MyRes = MyResource.new() # Cannot assign a new value to a constant.\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI've kind of describe them above, and I've also included an MRP below, which should hopefully clear things up more.\nWhen making a change to the C# side of the MRP, don't forget to re-compile and to save the GDScript script again.\nSometimes, the script editor might not update properly and won't show the error, but the Output tab will always have the error if it's there. You can always save the script to make the error show up in the Output tab.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[new-value-to-constant-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33151137/new-value-to-constant-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false